<h1 id="wo-04-reliable-ingestion-bounded-health-checks-comment-counts-and-program-alerts">WO-04 — Reliable ingestion, bounded health checks, comment counts and program alerts</h1>
<h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
<ul><li>Findings <strong>R09, R11, R12 and R13 remain OPEN</strong> against current source baseline <code>9fae324</code>. This is an English planning document, not implementation or closure evidence.</li><li>Sixteen atomic tasks, seven Evidence Waves, four contract rows, explicit write sets, independent review and QA. No source/test edits, test execution, deployment, data mutation or live messaging today.</li><li>Preserve existing Node22/ESM, Firestore roots, domain identities, authorization and durable delivery semantics. No new dependency by default; no exactly-once FCM claim.</li><li><strong>Policy gate:</strong> R13 conflicts with the automation contract's fixed Yemen date while the content contract and validator accept per-schedule UTC offsets. Approve the policy/ADR before implementing timezone or receipt changes. Preferred proposal: honor accepted per-schedule offsets with a reviewed compatibility cutover.</li><li>Highest risks: changed RSS identity causing duplicates, stale comment recount overwriting newer counts, and notification key migration resending acknowledged/unknown deliveries. Each has explicit bounded migration/rollback controls.</li></ul>
<h2 id="document-information">Document information</h2>
<ul><li>Date: 2026-10-25. Owner: Delivery Lead. Scope: <code>hudhud_fm</code> only.</li><li>Inputs: [technical review](tech-review.md), [content automation](../../docs/contracts/content-automation-contract.md), [station content](../../docs/contracts/station-content-contract.md), [data contract](../../docs/contracts/firebase-data-contract.md), [security](../../docs/contracts/security-privacy-contract.md).</li><li>Existing architecture is retained. No invented PRD or pre-existing new API/module is assumed. All new paths below are marked <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>.</li></ul>
<h2 id="0-repo-preflight-and-current-evidence">0. Repo Preflight and current evidence</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Fact</th><th>Evidence and implication</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Source baseline</td><td><code>9fae324</code>; earlier review baseline unchanged; current work is planning artifacts only</td></tr><tr><td>R09</td><td>[rss-ingestion.js:69](../../functions/lib/rss-ingestion.js:69) copies enclosure attributes without entity decoding; [line196](../../functions/lib/rss-ingestion.js:196) publishes the payload; deterministicEpisodeId/contentIdentity/importKeys/counters/audit must remain coherent</td></tr><tr><td>R11</td><td>[stream-health.js:180](../../functions/lib/stream-health.js:180) scans all stations sequentially; primary+backup can cost16 seconds; [index.js:787](../../functions/index.js:787) has300-second timeout and Dev-before-Official order</td></tr><tr><td>R12</td><td>[comment-moderation.js:170](../../functions/lib/comment-moderation.js:170) updates only comment; [admin-report-review.js:58](../../functions/lib/admin-report-review.js:58) separately decrements; [index.js:644](../../functions/index.js:644) separately counts then overwrites, exposing a race</td></tr><tr><td>R13</td><td>[program-notifications.js:45](../../functions/lib/program-notifications.js:45) ignores schedule offset; line115 uses global Aden time, line133 keys <code>[programId,YemenDate]</code>, line142 revalidates likewise, line164 writes compatibility stamp</td></tr><tr><td>Contract disagreement</td><td>Content contract line37 makes offset explicit and admin validator accepts−720..840; automation §3/durable amendment explicitly use YemenDate and Yemen schedule. Do not silently choose one</td></tr><tr><td>Existing repair precedent</td><td><code>tool/backfill_content_identities.mjs</code> and <code>tool/test/backfill_content_identities.test.mjs</code>: explicit project/root/parent, dry-run, reviewed report, backup, bounds and preconditions; inspect and reuse safe pure patterns, never run or copy destructive behavior blindly</td></tr><tr><td>Harness gap</td><td><code>tool/run-admin-emulator-tests.mjs:35</code> exports only four admin callables; actual comment event handlers are not registered. Merely enabling four PL03 tests would not prove the worker ran</td></tr><tr><td>Existing regression</td><td><code>web_admin/test/pl03-moderation.emulator.test.ts</code> contains new-comment and corrected-counter control cases for both roots; all four must execute, with new-comment evidence independent of manual count seeding</td></tr><tr><td>Tools/CI</td><td>Existing Functions built-in tests/lint, root Rules/admin/editorial/account-deletion/subscriptions emulator scripts; Node22 required. <code>.github/workflows</code> absent in earlier preflight; external CI unknown</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="1-design-impact-and-operational-boundaries">1. Design, impact and operational boundaries</h2>
<h3 id="1-1-r09-decode-safely-without-changing-historical-identity">1.1 R09 — decode safely without changing historical identity</h3>
<p>Decode the five predefined XML entities and valid decimal/hex numeric character references in attributes/text <strong>before URL validation and identity calculation</strong>. Reject invalid scalar values/malformed input according to explicit parser policy. No DTD expansion, external entity resolution or new network requests. Prefer a small tested helper in the existing module; add a parser dependency only if correctness cannot be achieved safely and after revising the impact plan.</p>
<p>Existing GUID-less feeds used raw URL text for fallback identity. Corrected decoding therefore must resolve both raw/normalized identity aliases against existing episodes/importKeys before creating anything. Preserve existing episode document IDs, counters, publication flags and audit history; reserve owned aliases to the same ID transactionally. Conflicting aliases stop for review; never merge distinct episodes automatically. Already-bad URLs get a separate reviewed bounded repair, not a broad reimport. Repair must not create/delete episodes, toggle publication, increment parent counts, or emit real publication notifications.</p>
<h3 id="1-2-r11-bounded-fair-progress">1.2 R11 — bounded fair progress</h3>
<p>Preserve sequential station probing and the shared maximum of four outbound fetches per instance; do not bypass <code>public-fetch.js</code> or its8-second deadline. <strong>Proposed budget:</strong>100 seconds per root, at least40 seconds reserved for flushing/cleanup within the existing300-second invocation limit. Before starting a primary+backup pair, require at least16 seconds plus a measured flush margin. If a future timeout changes, derive budget from the same constants.</p>
<p>Persist a private per-root cursor, lease/generation and last completed station ID. <strong>Proposed path:</strong> <code>{root}/streamHealthJobs/checkpoints/active</code>; clients of every role cannot read/write it. Stable document-ID paging must progress for &gt;100 stations and survive station deletion; skip missing records without recreating them. Concurrent invocations cannot both advance/overwrite progress. Keep zero writes to stable station documents under the existing heartbeat policy; checkpoint writes are a separately documented bounded operational exception, not disguised as zero total writes. Inject a clock/probe for deterministic budget tests.</p>
<h3 id="1-3-r12-one-count-authority">1.3 R12 — one count authority</h3>
<p><strong>Proposed module:</strong> <code>functions/lib/comment-counts.js</code>; <strong>proposed private ledger:</strong> <code>{root}/commentCountContributions/episodes/{episodeId}/comments/{commentId}</code>. Store only contribution/revision/state needed for correctness, no comment body/name/email. No client role may read/write the ledger or directly change counters.</p>
<p>One transaction protocol reads the current comment, episode and prior contribution before writes, calculates the delta between desired/current published contribution and ledger, and updates count/ledger atomically. Event retries/out-of-order events recompute from fresh current state instead of trusting event snapshots. Manual moderation passes its authorized intended transition through the same authority in the same transaction. Account deletion uses the same protocol when removing comments; remove the competing standalone decrement/recount-overwrite path. Never recreate a deleted episode/comment. Define deleted ledger cleanup and delayed-event handling in T01; active contributions cannot expire arbitrarily.</p>
<p>Backfill must initialize ledger and count consistently under a scoped write-quiescence window or a tested revision barrier. A plain aggregate count followed by overwrite is not sufficient. <strong>Proposed limit:</strong>25 items per invocation, explicit episode/root, resumable checkpoint, private before-images and conditional rollback of ledger/counter only—never restore deleted comments or overwrite current moderation. Large episodes require bounded pages plus a final revision-checked activation; no partial active baseline.</p>
<h3 id="1-4-r13-policy-decision-and-delivery-preserving-cutover">1.4 R13 — policy decision and delivery-preserving cutover</h3>
<p>Preferred approved semantics: eligibility weekday/minute/local date and operation key use each schedule's accepted UTC offset. Revalidate the schedule immediately before starting send; a concurrent schedule edit must not mutate an already-bound intent. Retain claim/start/finish, pending/failed/sent/unknown behavior; <strong>unknown never auto-retries</strong>.</p>
<p>Pause old/new workers during the key/date cutover, select a documented cutover day/window, and map old Yemen-date receipts to new local occurrences conservatively. Existing terminal sent/unknown receipts suppress duplicates, including ambiguous cross-midnight overlap. Do not delete receipts or reset lastNotifiedDate to force sends. Where mapping is ambiguous, suppress and require operator review; skipped historical delivery is safer than unauthorized repeat delivery. Rollback pauses workers and preserves both old/new receipt evidence; it does not blindly restore the old key scheme.</p>
<h3 id="1-5-blast-radius">1.5 Blast radius</h3>
<p>High: shared entry point, private state, counters, delivery identity, contracts, maintenance tools and emulator harness. All writes are enumerated below; no new packages or lockfiles planned. Any necessary index update is additive and reviewed by the shared integration owner after WO-03. Later production work is separately authorized; this planning request executes none of it.</p>
<h2 id="2-atomic-tasks">2. Atomic tasks</h2>
<p>Commands are planned <strong>red then green</strong> at the specified cwd. New test files must first be created with executable business assertions; a missing module/file, zero tests or a skip is not valid red evidence. Pure test seams may precede the red assertion but must not implement the fix covertly.</p>
<h3 id="04-t01-resolve-policy-and-approve-state-contracts">04-T01 — Resolve policy and approve state contracts</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Data Architect/Delivery Lead. Depends on WO-01 and WO-03 contract handoffs before shared edits. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>docs/decisions/0006-background-consistency-and-schedule-timezones.md</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>docs/contracts/content-automation-contract.md</code>; <code>docs/contracts/station-content-contract.md</code>; <code>docs/contracts/firebase-data-contract.md</code>.</li><li>Decide per-schedule vs fixed-Yemen policy, key/stamp migration, comment-ledger ownership, backfill barrier and health checkpoint exception/budgets. Align descriptions of initial comment status with current behavior; do not silently introduce pending moderation UX.</li><li>Acceptance: independent policy signoff; public/private schema and cutover states explicit; no R13 implementation before decision; operator can distinguish eligibility, send acknowledgement and device receipt.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t02-xml-decoding-and-backward-compatible-ingestion-identity">04-T02 — XML decoding and backward-compatible ingestion identity</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend RSS. Depends on T01. Complexity: medium/high.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/rss-ingestion.js</code>; <code>functions/test/rss-ingestion.test.js</code>; <code>functions/lib/admin-content-relations.js</code>; <code>functions/test/admin-content.test.js</code>.</li><li>Implement entity decoding and safe validation; resolve historical/raw and normalized aliases without replacing existing episode IDs; use existing reservation transaction pattern.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/rss-ingestion.test.js test/admin-content.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: <code>&amp;amp;</code>, predefined/numeric entities and signed query URLs work; DTD/external entity never fetched; malformed entities rejected predictably; GUID and GUID-less reimport creates zero duplicates and preserves counters/audit/publication state.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t03-preview-and-repair-existing-malformed-rss-urls">04-T03 — Preview and repair existing malformed RSS URLs</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Data Tools. Depends on T02. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>tool/repair_rss_urls.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>tool/test/repair_rss_urls.test.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>.</li><li>Read existing identity-backfill tool/tests for safe patterns; proposed repair defaults dry-run, one explicit root/program, manifest of raw/normalized identities and owned aliases, durable private backup before transaction.</li><li>Red/green, cwd root: <code>node --test tool/test/repair_rss_urls.test.mjs tool/test/backfill_content_identities.test.mjs</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: same episode ID before/after, zero new/deleted episodes, unchanged parent count/publication, alias conflicts fail closed, changed source skipped, resume idempotent, no real notification; rollback restores only owned fields conditionally and preserves alias safety.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t04-fair-bounded-stream-health-scanning">04-T04 — Fair bounded stream-health scanning</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend Health. Depends on T01. Complexity: medium.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/stream-health.js</code>; <code>functions/test/stream-health.test.js</code>.</li><li>Introduce injected clock/budget and bounded document-ID pages; stop before a pair would exhaust reserve; preserve sequential probe, backup logic, heartbeat and no raw URL logs.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/stream-health.test.js test/public-fetch.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance:19 dual8-second timeout fixtures cannot starve the second root; &gt;100 stations complete across finite invocations; stable station fields remain zero-write except documented heartbeat; global outbound cap unchanged.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t05-persist-health-leases-cursors-and-integrate-scheduler">04-T05 — Persist health leases/cursors and integrate scheduler</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend Health; Integration Owner lands entry-point edits. Depends on T04 and WO-01→WO-03 entry-point handoff. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/stream-health-progress.js</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>functions/test/stream-health-progress.test.js</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>functions/lib/stream-health.js</code>; <code>functions/index.js</code>.</li><li>Implement private per-root leased cursor; make scheduler give both roots their fair bounded budget; deterministic replay/expired-lease recovery, missing-station skip, checkpoint after successful unit.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/stream-health-progress.test.js test/stream-health.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: two workers cannot lose/regress cursor; timeout/resume advances; deleted cursor station does not block progress; checkpoint write count bounded and distinguished from station writes. Rollback pauses worker, never blindly erases cursor/lease.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t06-single-idempotent-comment-count-authority">04-T06 — Single idempotent comment-count authority</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend Counts. Depends on T01. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/comment-counts.js</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>functions/test/comment-counts.test.js</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>functions/lib/comment-moderation.js</code>; <code>functions/test/comment-moderation.test.js</code>.</li><li>Define pure transition planning plus read-before-write transaction helper, fresh-state contribution ledger and missing-episode behavior. Automatic moderation transitions use the same authority.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/comment-counts.test.js test/comment-moderation.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: published creation increments once; rejected/hidden/removed/deleted subtract once; duplicate/out-of-order events converge, count never negative, missing episodes never recreated; no comment body or PII in ledger.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t07-integrate-manual-moderation-deletion-and-real-event-handler">04-T07 — Integrate manual moderation, deletion and real event handler</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Shared Integration Owner with Backend Counts. Depends on T05,T06 and WO-01/WO-03 shared handoffs. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/index.js</code>; <code>functions/lib/admin-report-review.js</code>; <code>functions/lib/admin-content-delete.js</code>; <code>functions/test/admin-report-review.test.js</code>; <code>firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/account-deletion.test.js</code>.</li><li>Register an actual retry-safe on-write/delete count handler as proposed in T01; remove separate manual decrement and unsafe recount overwrite. Manual review and account deletion invoke the same count protocol; unrelated account cleanup stays intact.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/admin-report-review.test.js test/admin-content-delete.test.js test/comment-counts.test.js</code>; cwd root: <code>npm run emulators:account-deletion</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: concurrent review/delete/event yields exact published count in both roots, deletion barriers preserved, no resurrected episode/comment, no double decrement; episode-ledger cleanup is safe for delayed events.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t08-make-the-actual-worker-observable-in-emulator-regressions">04-T08 — Make the actual worker observable in emulator regressions</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Integration Test Engineer. Depends on T07. Complexity: medium.</li><li>Write set: <code>tool/run-admin-emulator-tests.mjs</code>; <code>web_admin/test/pl03-moderation.emulator.test.ts</code>; <code>firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/editorial-comment-counts.test.js</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>.</li><li>Extend the temp Functions harness to export the actual new count event handler and relevant existing moderation handler, not just four callables. Keep Gemini/network senders disabled or injected deterministic mocks; no developer secrets loaded.</li><li>Red/green, cwd root: <code>npm run emulators:admin</code>; <code>npm run emulators:editorial</code> for standalone Firestore fixtures; worker registration must be demonstrated by the admin harness journey.</li><li>Acceptance: all4 PL03 cases actually run, including two new-comment journeys; corrected-counter controls remain separate, never substituted for missing automatic count. Wait boundedly for the real trigger result, no arbitrary fixed sleeps or manual expected-counter seeding in new-comment cases.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t09-bounded-comment-ledger-baseline-reconciliation">04-T09 — Bounded comment-ledger baseline/reconciliation</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Data Tools. Depends on T06–T08. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>tool/reconcile_comment_counts.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>tool/test/reconcile_comment_counts.test.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md</code>.</li><li>Explicit project/root/episode; preview count/contribution inventory, private durable backup, write-quiescence or revision barrier, staged bounded ledger baseline and atomic activation. Proposed25-item invocation bound with resume.</li><li>Red/green, cwd root: <code>node --test tool/test/reconcile_comment_counts.test.mjs</code> and demo fixture T08.</li><li>Acceptance: live edit during preview/apply invalidates baseline or retries through barrier; no mixed partially active ledger; final counter equals published query count; restore only owned ledger/counter state if expected revision matches, never comment content/moderation or deleted records.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t10-implement-approved-per-schedule-timing-and-intent-identity">04-T10 — Implement approved per-schedule timing and intent identity</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Backend Notifications. Depends on approved T01 policy. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>functions/lib/program-notifications.js</code>; <code>functions/test/program-notifications.test.js</code>; <code>functions/test/notification-delivery.test.js</code>.</li><li>Compute eligibility/local date/key/stamp consistently from approved policy; bind schedule revision/fingerprint to intent and revalidate before send; preserve delivery protocol.</li><li>Red/green, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>node --test test/program-notifications.test.js test/notification-delivery.test.js</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: UTC Monday10:00 not eligible07:00Z but eligible10:00Z; UTC+3, negative offset, midnight/weekdays, schedule edits and concurrent workers covered; one intent per approved occurrence, unknown never auto-retried, no exactly-once transport claim.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t11-receipt-aware-timezone-cutover-and-rollback">04-T11 — Receipt-aware timezone cutover and rollback</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Data Tools/Notifications. Depends on T10 and approved T01 cutover. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>tool/migrate_program_notification_dates.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>tool/test/migrate_program_notification_dates.test.mjs</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong>; <code>docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md</code>.</li><li>Proposed CLI defaults dry-run and explicit root/program/date range. Quiesce old/new workers, review mapping of old Yemen receipts to new occurrences, privately back up receipt/key state, reserve aliases or suppression state without resetting history.</li><li>Red/green, cwd root: <code>node --test tool/test/migrate_program_notification_dates.test.mjs</code>; Functions delivery tests remain required.</li><li>Acceptance: terminal sent/unknown receipts suppress duplicate send through cutover and rollback; cross-day ambiguity stops/suppresses for review; never delete old receipts or reset compatibility stamps to force send; no live FCM in tests.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t12-private-state-authorization-and-query-index-integration">04-T12 — Private-state authorization and query/index integration</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Shared Integration Owner. Depends on T05,T07,T08,T11 and WO-01→WO-03 Rules/index handoff. T08→T12 explicitly serializes the shared editorial-comment-counts fixture. Complexity: medium.</li><li>Write set: <code>firestore.rules</code>; <code>firebase_tests/firebase-rules/firestore.rules.test.js</code>; <code>firestore.indexes.json</code> <strong>only if actual query requires a missing index</strong>; <code>firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/editorial-comment-counts.test.js</code>.</li><li>Default deny should already protect new paths; add explicit regression coverage without broad allow rules. Role-denial tests use client SDKs even when carrying admin/super-admin claims; trusted Admin SDK workers bypass Rules and must instead be checked through server authorization and explicit root validation. Determine exact indexes from implemented queries and add only necessary definitions.</li><li>Red/green, cwd root: <code>npm run emulators:test</code>; <code>npm run emulators:editorial</code>.</li><li>Acceptance: checkpoint/contribution/notification receipts denied to guest, listener, scoped admin, super-admin and forged claims in both roots; unknown roots denied; clients cannot write episode counts; public data and existing authorized workflows preserved. Record no index change if none is necessary.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t13-independent-exact-candidate-qa">04-T13 — Independent exact-candidate QA</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: QA independent of implementers. Depends on T02–T12. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>.boss/technical-review/WO-04-validation.md</code> <strong>PROPOSED NEW</strong> only; failed tests return to owning task for changes.</li><li>Verify exact candidate commit after shared integration, record Node22 version, commands, counts/skips and source hash. No production/messaging.</li><li>Planned commands, cwd <code>functions</code>: <code>npm run lint</code>, <code>npm test</code>. Cwd root: <code>npm run emulators:test</code>, <code>npm run emulators:admin</code>, <code>npm run emulators:editorial</code>, <code>npm run emulators:account-deletion</code>, <code>npm run emulators:subscriptions</code>; all new tool unit commands from T03/T09/T11. Admin test/lint if harness or types changed.</li><li>Acceptance: zero relevant failures/skips, real worker journey observed, all four matrix rows evidenced, &gt;100-station finite progress and all count/receipt concurrency cases pass; unrelated private-field/email safeguards from WO-01 remain intact.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t14-independent-code-and-migration-review">04-T14 — Independent code and migration review</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Tech Lead not an implementation author. Depends on T13. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>.boss/technical-review/WO-04-validation.md</code> only, serial after QA.</li><li>Review actual diff against write sets, authority/privacy, query/index necessity, identity ownership, event ordering, migration/rollback and approved ADR. Verify tests assert business behavior, not only mocks matching implementation.</li><li>Acceptance: no unresolved high-impact finding, no unexpected dependency/config changes, every query/worker has bounded lifecycle, evidence matches candidate commit. Changes after review invalidate affected checks.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t15-rehearse-safe-operations-and-prepare-concrete-approval">04-T15 — Rehearse safe operations and prepare concrete approval</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Operations Lead plus independent QA. Depends on T14. Complexity: high.</li><li>Write set: <code>docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md</code>; <code>.boss/technical-review/WO-04-validation.md</code>.</li><li>Demo-only rehearsal of RSS alias repair, count baseline, health resume and notification cutover, including interrupted apply/recovery. Prepare actual root-scoped manifests, backup locations/retention and compatible deployment sequence for later authorization.</li><li>Acceptance: verified private backups precede writes, bounded operations converge, conditional restore works, no duplicate push or public sensitive-data restoration; production action remains pending applicable authorization.</li></ul>
<h3 id="04-t16-later-authorized-rollout-and-finding-closure">04-T16 — Later authorized rollout and finding closure</h3>
<ul><li>Owner: Operations Lead. Depends on T15 and explicit applicable authorization. Complexity: high.</li><li>File write set: operational document and WO-04 validation report only; environment mutation restricted to approved manifests.</li><li>Quiesce incompatible workers, deploy compatible reviewed versions, execute one root/operation at a time, verify counts/identities/cursors/receipts and independent QA evidence. Keep uncertain delivery suppressed.</li><li>Acceptance: R09/R11/R12/R13 close individually only when their source and scoped operational criteria are proven. Otherwise retain OPEN or documented residual scope; never claim migration success from a code-only test.</li></ul>
<h2 id="3-pre-execution-checklist-and-migration-safeguards">3. Pre-execution checklist and migration safeguards</h2>
<ul><li>Recheck current commit, user edits, AGENTS, contracts and worker definitions; no dispatch on stale evidence.</li><li>Approve R13 policy/ADR and count-ledger baseline/cleanup rules before code. No silent change from YemenDate.</li><li>Compute write-set union and authorize high-impact implementation according to current user authorization. This document alone grants none.</li><li>Every migration proposed above requires explicit project/one root/scope, dry-run default, deterministic reviewed manifest with schema/version/hash and expected source fingerprint, durable private backup verified before mutation, batches of at most25 transactions/concurrency1 by default, resumable lease/checkpoint and conditional restore.</li><li>Backups live outside Git and <code>.boss</code>, contain minimum necessary restricted data, have least-privilege encrypted storage and defined retention. Reports contain counts/status/hashes only, no URLs/tokens/comment content/email.</li><li>Wrong project/root, missing backup, source change, ownership conflict, unknown schema or lost lease stops mutation. No broad delete/update or automatic merge of conflicting identities.</li><li>RSS rollback cannot create/delete/re-publish episodes; count rollback cannot restore comments or stale moderation; notification rollback cannot reset sent/unknown receipts or resend. Health rollback pauses worker and preserves cursor evidence.</li><li>All rollback tooling must preserve WO-01 privacy changes: never restore private station fields to public documents or email to listener profiles from older backups.</li><li>Retain existing authentication, deletion barriers, delivery privacy and public-fetch SSRF/deadline protections. No real Gemini/Telegram/email/FCM as an implicit verification step.</li></ul>
<h2 id="4-dependency-graph-and-evidence-waves">4. Dependency graph and Evidence Waves</h2>
<h3 id="4-1-shared-file-ownership-and-safe-parallel-work">4.1 Shared-file ownership and safe parallel work</h3>
<p>T01 gates every branch. RSS T02→T03; health T04→T05; counts T06→T07→T08→T09; notifications T10→T11. T07 waits T05 because both modify <code>index.js</code>; T12 waits private schema branches and T08 fixture ownership; T13→T14→T15→T16 closes integration. T03→T09→T11 operational-document edits are serial even when module work is parallel.</p>
<p>After approved T01, disjoint module tasks T02, T04, T06 and T10 may run alongside disjoint work in other WOs. T05 cannot run concurrently with T04 because both write stream-health; T07 waits all prior shared index ownership. No overlap is permitted merely because tasks are in different Waves.</p>
<p><strong>Handoff is not final acceptance:</strong> WO-04 waits only for WO-01/WO-03 approved contract and shared-source-file handoffs, not their full work-order closure. These are INTERIM handoffs with scoped checks; they do not mark an unfinished QA task or Evidence Wave complete. WO-03 final acceptance needs the actual PL03 worker delivered by04-T08, so requiring WO-03 closure before04-T08 would create a forbidden cycle. Likewise, WO-01 integration QA may wait for this worker; WO-01 need not be globally CLOSED before WO-03 starts disjoint authorized work. After integration, rerun the complete required suite—including all17 previously skipped admin emulator checks—before closing affected QA/Waves/findings.</p>
<p>Central integration order: <code>functions/index.js</code> <strong>WO-01→WO-03→WO-04</strong>; Rules/tests and shared contracts use the same reviewed handoff order where touched; <code>firestore.indexes.json</code> <strong>WO-03→WO-04</strong>, additive only if necessary. <code>admin-app.tsx</code>/Excel remain owned by WO-01→WO-03 and are not WO-04 write sets. The emulator harness has one owner, T08; later QA is read-only unless defects return to T08. Rebase and revalidate after each shared handoff.</p>
