<h3 id="4-3-contract-matrix">4.3 Contract Matrix</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>ID</th><th>UI/contract and enum semantics</th><th>Payload/schema/persistence</th><th>Business rule</th><th>Planned evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CM09 (R09)</td><td>Playable original enclosure semantics; existing episode links stable</td><td>Decoded5+numeric entities; validated URL; raw/normalized aliases owned by same existing ID</td><td>No DTD/external fetch; no duplicate episode, count change or republish</td><td>rss-ingestion/admin-content + repair/backfill tests; alias conflict/resume fixtures</td></tr><tr><td>CM11 (R11)</td><td>Health online/degraded/offline and heartbeat unchanged</td><td>Existing probe8s and outboundmax4; proposed per-root100s/flush40s; private cursor+lease</td><td>Both roots progress within300s; stable station no-write except heartbeat; checkpoints explicitly bounded</td><td>Injected clock19dual-timeout/&gt;100station/reclaim/deletedstation tests; private Rules denial</td></tr><tr><td>CM12 (R12)</td><td>Displayed commentsCount equals current published comments</td><td>Single transaction authority and private contribution ledger; published/hidden/removed/rejected/deleted semantics</td><td>Fresh-state delta idempotent; no negative count or resurrection; barrier-protected baseline</td><td>Both-root real PL03 new-comment/control tests, duplicate/out-of-order/concurrent moderation/deletion, reconciliation crash tests</td></tr><tr><td>CM13 (R13)</td><td>Schedule time and notification local-date semantics match approved ADR</td><td>Offset accepted range and revalidated schedule; compatible receipt key/stamp mapping</td><td>One intent per approved occurrence; sent/unknown preserved; no auto-retry unknown or exactly-once claim</td><td>UTC/+3/negative/midnight/edit/concurrent worker + durable delivery/cutover tests; private receipt denial</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Every row is <strong>PLANNED / UNVERIFIED in this session</strong>. Historical review tests establish defects, not completion of this work order.</p>
<h2 id="5-file-summary">5. File summary</h2>
<h3 id="5-1-proposed-new-files-only">5.1 Proposed new files only</h3>
<p><code>docs/decisions/0006-background-consistency-and-schedule-timezones.md</code>; <code>docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md</code>; <code>functions/lib/stream-health-progress.js</code>; <code>functions/test/stream-health-progress.test.js</code>; <code>functions/lib/comment-counts.js</code>; <code>functions/test/comment-counts.test.js</code>; <code>tool/repair_rss_urls.mjs</code>; <code>tool/test/repair_rss_urls.test.mjs</code>; <code>tool/reconcile_comment_counts.mjs</code>; <code>tool/test/reconcile_comment_counts.test.mjs</code>; <code>tool/migrate_program_notification_dates.mjs</code>; <code>tool/test/migrate_program_notification_dates.test.mjs</code>; <code>firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/editorial-comment-counts.test.js</code>; <code>.boss/technical-review/WO-04-validation.md</code>.</p>
<h3 id="5-2-existing-files-and-serialization">5.2 Existing files and serialization</h3>
<p>Task write sets are authoritative and contain at most5 paths per task. Shared index T05→T07; health T04→T05; operational document T03→T09→T11→T15→T16; validation T13→T14→T15→T16. Rules/index integration occurs after WO-01/WO-03. Existing <code>tool/backfill_content_identities.mjs</code> is a read-only reference unless separately justified and planned; no destructive reuse is assumed.</p>
<h3 id="5-3-verification-scope">5.3 Verification scope</h3>
<p>Node22 Functions unit/lint; existing real emulator scripts and proposed tool tests; tests must identify actual candidate commit and distinguish mocks, emulator worker execution and production evidence. No dependency audit claim, build success, device acceptance, migration execution or production sending is inferred from this plan.</p>
<h2 id="6-standards-and-closure">6. Standards and closure</h2>
<p>Preserve current architecture and error/privacy conventions. Bound queries, retries, scan deadlines and state retention; use transaction reads before writes. Never log raw stream URLs, tokens, account data or comment content. Required QA/reviewer independence is a gate, not self-approval by implementers. Findings remain OPEN until the corresponding fix and authorized operational scope meet their measurable acceptance criteria.</p>
